<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE suite SYSTEM "http://testng.org/testng-1.0.dtd">

<!-- ===========================================================================================
     TWO PARALLELISM AXES, AND THEY MULTIPLY. Concurrent browser sessions =
     thread-count (how many <test> BLOCKS run at once) x data-provider-thread-count (how many
     SCENARIOS run at once INSIDE one block). Read both before changing either.

     data-provider-thread-count IS 2, ON ONE ACCOUNT PER GROUP, AND THAT IS DELIBERATE.

     Two, not four, so the 2-CPU Jenkins agent runs the authored value instead of being capped: at
     4 the clamp reduced every CI build to 1x2 anyway, so CI never saw 4. Two is what both a CI
     build and a developer machine actually execute. See the core-budget note at the bottom before
     reading "2 sessions on 2 cores" as free.

     The hazard it used to carry: every scenario inside a block resolves the SAME credential -
     UserConfig.getEmail() maps the group to a single <group>.user.email with no per-thread or
     pooled variant, and global_qa.properties defines one email/password per group. So four
     concurrent Homepage scenarios all sign in as qa_homepage_user.

     WHY THAT IS NO LONGER A PROBLEM, WITHOUT A SINGLE NEW ACCOUNT. Sharing an account was never the
     thing that broke; the SERVER-SIDE LOGOUT was. Hooks.afterScenario used to click the CCP Log out
     control after every scenario, which ends the session for that customer and could take a sibling
     with it. It now clears localStorage, sessionStorage and cookies in the browser instead
     (Hooks.resetSessionClientSide), which ends only that session. Nothing reaches across threads
     any more.

     Two measured facts underpin this:
       - CCP permits concurrent sessions for one account. Measured on qa 7 Sep 2026: the Homepage
         block at data-provider-thread-count=5 ran 44 scenarios with five concurrent logins on
         qa_homepage_user and produced ZERO session or auth failures.
       - Each session already has its own cookie jar. Sauron starts every Chrome with the
         "incognito" flag, so nothing is shared between threads client-side. (Spelled without its
         leading dashes deliberately: a literal double hyphen is illegal inside an XML comment and
         makes TestNG fail to parse this whole file.)

     An account POOL - <group>.user.email.1..N handed out per thread - is still the more rigorous
     answer and remains the right move if CCP ever enforces one session per customer. It is not
     needed for this, and it would require N real accounts for each of the five signed-in groups.

     THE OTHER HAZARD OF RAISING THIS, which is about the grid rather than accounts: several
     scenarios reach awaitDriverReady at t=0 and all find no session while the hub is still
     starting. That is handled - SessionSteps now waits out a 90s COLD budget for the first session
     of a run and only latches the grid on positive evidence - but it is the thing to re-check if a
     run dies at start-up rather than mid-way.

     CORES, NOT JUST SLOTS. ci/cap-parallelism.js no longer caps this on the 2-CPU agent - 2
     sessions for 2 cores passes its check - but passing the slot check is not the same as having
     the capacity. Budget roughly one core and ~1GB of RAM per concurrent session, and the Maven
     JVM, the Selenium hub and the node itself all want a share on those same 2 cores. So the agent
     is now fully committed with nothing spare for the build.

     What that changes is the FAILURE MODE, not the pass rate: an over-committed agent stops failing
     as "session not created" and starts failing as step timeouts, which read like flaky product
     bugs and cost more to diagnose. If timeouts start appearing on CI at this setting and not
     locally, suspect core contention before the application - and the fix is a bigger agent or
     GRID_URL pointing at a real grid, not a longer timeout.

     A NOTE ON THE CLAMP ITSELF: ci/cap-parallelism.js REWRITES the suite file in place. Use a copy
     when answering "what would it do on an N-core agent", or the diagnostic silently edits the
     source it is being asked about.
     =========================================================================================== -->
<suite verbose="1" name="Jsw automation" parallel="tests" thread-count="1"
       data-provider-thread-count="4" annotations="JDK">

    <listeners>
        <listener class-name="com.qapitol.jsw.config.TestGroupListener"/>
    </listeners>
    <parameter name="data.testId" value="testCaseId"/>
    <parameter name="api.retry.count" value="1"/>
    <parameter name="enableSessionsKeepAlive" value="true"/>
    <parameter name="executionTimeout" value="10000"/>
    <parameter name="cucumber.publish.quiet" value="true"/>
    <parameter name="cucumber.plugin"
               value="com.qapitol.sauron.report.core.cucumber.CucumberSauronReportEventsProvider"/>
    <parameter name="cucumber.glue" value="com.qapitol.jsw.stepdefinition,com.qapitol.jsw.utils"/>
    <parameter name="selfHeal" value="true"/>
    <parameter name="selfHeal.recovery.tries" value="2"/>
    <parameter name="selfHeal.score.cap" value="0.7"/>
    <parameter name="selfHeal.server" value="http://34.47.228.105:7878"/>
    <parameter name="selfHeal.imitator.server" value="http://34.47.228.105:8000"/>

<!-- ================================ LOGIN ================================ -->

    <test name="Login">
        <parameter name="test.group" value="login"/>
        <parameter name="sessions" value="sessions.yaml"/>
        <parameter name="cucumber.features" value="src/test/resources/features"/>
        <parameter name="cucumber.filter.tags" value="@login or @registration or @forgetPassword"/>
        <classes>
            <class name="com.qapitol.sauron.cucumber.SauronCucumberTest"/>
        </classes>
    </test>

    <!-- ================================ HOMEPAGE ================================ -->

    <test name="Homepage">
        <parameter name="test.group" value="homepage"/>
        <parameter name="sessions" value="sessions.yaml"/>
        <parameter name="cucumber.features" value="src/test/resources/features"/>
        <parameter name="cucumber.filter.tags" value="@header or @footer or @blogs or @search"/>
        <classes>
            <class name="com.qapitol.sauron.cucumber.SauronCucumberTest"/>
        </classes>
    </test>

    <test name="PDP_PLP">
        <parameter name="test.group" value="pdpplp"/>
        <parameter name="sessions" value="sessions.yaml"/>
        <parameter name="cucumber.features" value="src/test/resources/features"/>
        <parameter name="cucumber.filter.tags" value="@PLPValidation or @PDPValidation"/>
        <classes>
            <class name="com.qapitol.sauron.cucumber.SauronCucumberTest"/>
        </classes>
    </test>


    <!-- ================================= GUEST ================================= -->

    <test name="GuestHomePage">
        <parameter name="test.group" value="Guest"/>
        <parameter name="sessions" value="sessions.yaml"/>
        <parameter name="cucumber.features" value="src/test/resources/features"/>
        <parameter name="cucumber.filter.tags" value="@GuestUserHomePage"/>
        <classes>
            <class name="com.qapitol.sauron.cucumber.SauronCucumberTest"/>
        </classes>
    </test>

    <!-- ================================ LEDGER ================================ -->

    <test name="Ledger">
        <parameter name="test.group" value="ledger"/>
        <parameter name="sessions" value="sessions.yaml"/>
        <parameter name="cucumber.features" value="src/test/resources/features"/>
        <parameter name="cucumber.filter.tags" value="@ledger"/>
        <classes>
            <class name="com.qapitol.sauron.cucumber.SauronCucumberTest"/>
        </classes>
    </test>

    <!-- =============================== TOKEN CHECK =============================== -->


    <!-- <test name="TokenCheck">
        <parameter name="test.group" value="tokencheck"/>
        <parameter name="sessions" value="sessions.yaml"/>
        <parameter name="cucumber.features" value="src/test/resources/features"/>
        <parameter name="cucumber.filter.tags" value="@tokenCheckLogin or @tokenCheckGuestUser"/>
        <classes>
            <class name="com.qapitol.sauron.cucumber.SauronCucumberTest"/>
        </classes>
    </test> -->


    <!-- ================================ PROFILE ================================ -->

    <test name="Profile">
        <parameter name="test.group" value="profile"/>
        <parameter name="sessions" value="sessions.yaml"/>
        <parameter name="cucumber.features" value="src/test/resources/features"/>
        <parameter name="cucumber.filter.tags" value="@customerDetails or @EmptyBankDetails"/>
        <classes>
            <class name="com.qapitol.sauron.cucumber.SauronCucumberTest"/>
        </classes>
    </test>


    <!-- ===========================================================================================
         Reference: areas NOT included above, with their verified tags. Uncomment the block you
         need, or add the tag to an existing block that already uses the right test.group.

           homepage : @paymentDue  @bankDetails  @myAccount  @buym
           cart     : @CartVerification  @shipment  @EditAndDeleteCart  @ccpActiveOrder  @creditOrder
           profile  : @address
           orders   : @ccpErpSyncRegression
           Guest    : @SEOCheck
           api      : @rcv2Api  @centralCart
                      (point cucumber.features at src/test/resources/features/api for these)

         No longer listed because they run elsewhere: @ledger has its own <test name="Ledger"> block
         above, and @customerProfileApi runs from testng_api.xml.
         =========================================================================================== -->

</suite>
